---
import CommunityLayout from '../components/CommunityLayout.astro';
import { TOOLS } from '../lib/tools';
---

<CommunityLayout
  title="About iDuckIMG: who runs it, what it costs, how it is built"
  description="iDuckIMG is a free set of image tools that run in your browser. Learn who runs it, what it costs and how your files are handled."
  before="About"
  mark="iDuckIMG"
  intro={`${TOOLS.length} free image tools that run in your browser, from the makers of iDuckPDF.`}
>
  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="files">
    <h2 id="files" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">What happens to your files</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      Every tool runs in your browser. Your pictures are opened, changed and saved on your own device, and they are not
      uploaded to our servers. Our host, Cloudflare, sees the same ordinary web requests for our pages that any website
      sees. Please do not rely on that alone for anything truly secret: check any tool you trust, and close the tab when you
      are done.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="who">
    <h2 id="who" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Who runs it</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      iDuckIMG is made and run by Basic App Company. It is a sister site of
      <a class="link" href="https://iduckpdf.com/" rel="noopener">iDuckPDF</a>, which has free PDF tools, and shares its look.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="cost">
    <h2 id="cost" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">What it costs</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      Nothing. There is no sign-up and no watermark on your results. We may show ads to cover the running costs, and we will
      keep them away from the upload area and the download button. See <a class="link" href="/support/">Support</a> for ways
      to help.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="built">
    <h2 id="built" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">How it is built</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      The pages are plain static files made with Astro, with small Preact pieces for the tools. The heavy lifting is done by
      open-source code compiled to WebAssembly and run in a background worker in your browser: jSquash for JPG, PNG and WebP,
      libheif for iPhone HEIC photos, and pdf-lib for PDFs. Because everything runs on your device, large photos can take a
      moment on an older phone.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Get in touch</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      The easiest way is the <a class="link" href="/feedback/">feedback form</a>. To ask for a tool, use
      <a class="link" href="/request/">Request a feature</a>. You can also write to Basic App Company at
      <a class="link" href="mailto:hello@iduckimg.com">hello@iduckimg.com</a>. See also
      <a class="link" href="/how-it-works/">How iDuckIMG works</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</CommunityLayout>
